{
  "id": "python_py_fastapi_first_api",
  "title": "Your first FastAPI endpoint",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "testId": "python_test_py_fastapi_first_api_en",
  "estimatedMinutes": 20,
  "sources": [
    "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/first-steps/",
    "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/deployment/manually/"
  ],
  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHY USE THIS?\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI builds JSON APIs that web and mobile applications call over HTTP; type annotations help validate inputs and describe the API contract.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PURPOSE AND REAL-WORLD USE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "We will build the first API end to end: the FastAPI app accepts a GET request at ",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "/",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and returns a greeting as JSON. GET is used to read information; browsers, mobile apps, and other services call endpoints like this.\n\n",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "To run these examples locally, install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "pip install fastapi uvicorn httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " plus any extra package named in the lesson. Save the server example as ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app.py",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and start ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "uvicorn app:app --reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "--reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is for development only.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHERE DOES THIS APPEAR IN REAL LIFE?\nA phone app can call this endpoint to check service availability or fetch public information for a landing page.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If this part is omitted: Without the ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " application there is nowhere to register routes. Without ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/\")",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", the function remains ordinary Python code and is not connected to an HTTP ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "GET /",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " request.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE EXAMPLE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"Hello API\", version=\"1.0.0\")\n\n@app.get(\"/\", tags=[\"Getting started\"])\nasync def read_root():\n    return {\n        \"message\": \"Hello, world!\",\n        \"lesson\": \"First API\"\n    }\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "REQUEST AND EXPECTED RESPONSE\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Request: GET /\nResponse: 200 OK; JSON: {\"message\":\"Salam, dünya!\",\"lesson\":\"First API\"}",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports FastAPI so the program can create its application object; without it, ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is undefined.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI(title=\"Hello API\", version=\"1.0.0\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/\", tags=[\"Getting started\"])",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def read_root():",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "\"message\": \"Hello, world!\",",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — This dictionary key becomes a field in the JSON response; changing it changes what API clients receive.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "\"lesson\": \"First API\"",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — This dictionary key becomes a field in the JSON response; changing it changes what API clients receive.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Continues the application's data handling or control flow.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "id": "fastapi_request",
      "caption": "A browser or mobile app sends GET /; FastAPI calls the matching function and returns a JSON response."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PRACTICE: CHECK IT WITH AN HTTP CLIENT\n",
      "size": 19,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This complete file calls the app locally with TestClient; it does not open a server port. Install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for TestClient.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE CLIENT TEST\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"Hello API\", version=\"1.0.0\")\n\n@app.get(\"/\", tags=[\"Getting started\"])\nasync def read_root():\n    return {\n        \"message\": \"Hello, world!\",\n        \"lesson\": \"First API\"\n    }\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n\nwith TestClient(app) as client:\n    response = client.get(\"/\")\n    print(response.status_code, response.json())\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXPECTED CLIENT-TEST OUTPUT\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "200 {'message': 'Hello, world!', 'lesson': 'First API'}",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports FastAPI so the program can create its application object; without it, ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is undefined.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI(title=\"Hello API\", version=\"1.0.0\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/\", tags=[\"Getting started\"])",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def read_root():",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "\"message\": \"Hello, world!\",",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — This dictionary key becomes a field in the JSON response; changing it changes what API clients receive.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "\"lesson\": \"First API\"",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — This dictionary key becomes a field in the JSON response; changing it changes what API clients receive.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Continues the application's data handling or control flow.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi.testclient import TestClient",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports TestClient so an HTTP request can exercise the app without opening a server port.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "with TestClient(app) as client:",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Creates a test HTTP client for the app and closes it when the context ends.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "response = client.get(\"/\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Sends the stated GET request through the test client and stores the response.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "print(response.status_code, response.json())",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Reads and prints both the HTTP status code and parsed JSON response.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMMON MISTAKES\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#C62828",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Calling an ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " function directly may give you a coroutine rather than the HTTP response. Call the endpoint through the server or an HTTP test client.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "title": "Practical tip",
      "text": "Start the server with `fastapi dev main.py`; open `GET /` in `/docs` and use **Try it out** to send a request."
    },
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "title": "One level deeper",
      "text": "`@app.get` binds the URL and HTTP method to the function; FastAPI converts the returned dictionary to JSON. The endpoint is not called until an HTTP request arrives."
    },
    {
      "type": "warning",
      "title": "Important warning",
      "text": "The example has no authentication or database. Design authorization, persistence, and HTTPS before exposing a public API."
    },
    {
